			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 3 components\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to 6b50bc7 bringing coordinated changes:\n- Mountain: Streamline extension path and NodeResolver module documentation — simplify ScanPathConfigure comments, condense NodeResolver docstring to compact resolution order ladder. No runtime changes.\n- Wind: Split monolithic PostHogBridge.ts into modular components under Source/Telemetry/PostHog/ — Browser.ts (window.posthog lookup), Configuration.ts (import.meta.env config), Fallback.ts (fetch POST fallback), Identifier.ts (distinct_id resolution), Properties.ts (base event properties). PostHogBridge.ts now composes these for improved testability.\n- Cocoon: Submodule updated to 33544546.\n\nThis coordinated update delivers documentation improvements and modular telemetry architecture while maintaining identical runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "083837fae5efc9f6c5264746397a010162832760"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T16:05:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				10
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add PostHog telemetry across all Land tiers\n\nIntroduce end-to-end PostHog telemetry pipeline for comprehensive editor analytics:\n\n- Add `.env.Land.PostHog.Sample` configuration template with per-element enable flags (MOUNTAIN, COCOON, WIND, SKY, BUILD), client-side rate limiting for Sky, session-recording/survey toggles, and distinct-ID seeding for CI correlation.\n\n- Add `Maintain/Script/PostHogCapture.sh` (Atom PH5) providing PostHogCapture function for build scripts to emit events like `build:start`, `build:ok`, `build:failed`. Silently tolerant of upstream failures to never block builds.\n\n- Update `TierEnvironment.sh` to source PostHog overlay and filter PostHog env vars in debug output.\n\n- Update `.gitignore` to exclude all PostHog env files.\n\n- Element submodule brings PostHog config to Mountain (build.rs env! macro), Sky (client-side rate limiting), and Wind (telemetry bridge reusing Sky's window.posthog instance).\n\nAll tiers now emit to a single PostHog project with `$component` and `$tier` properties for cross-tier session analysis.",
			"SHA": "f9ba655b121c843336cdea6c0f99f7d1fd2485a1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T14:23:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				98,
				9
			],
			"Message": "build(Land): Add domain-specific environment overlays and Node resolver support\n\nIntroduce .env.Land.Node.Sample and .env.Land.Extensions.Sample configuration\ntemplates with corresponding TierEnvironment.sh overlay loading. This enables:\n- Explicit Node binary override (LAND_NODE_BINARY) for reproducible builds\n- Minimum Node version enforcement (LAND_NODE_MIN_MAJOR=20)\n- Custom extension directory paths (LAND_USER_EXTENSIONS_DIR, LAND_EXTRA_EXTENSIONS_DIRS,\n  LAND_DEV_EXTENSIONS_DIR, LAND_BUILTIN_EXTENSIONS_DIR)\n- Built-in extension disable toggle (LAND_DISABLE_BUILTIN_EXTENSIONS)\n- Auto-install toggle for extension dependencies (LAND_AUTO_INSTALL_EXTENSION_DEPS)\n\nCoordinate Element submodule update across 12 components: Mountain adds Node binary\nresolver and extension path env vars; Sky implements lifecycle phase signaling;\nCocoon, Echo, Wind, Worker update dependencies; Mist, Output, Rest normalize CHANGELOG formatting.\n\nMinor CHANGELOG and Maintain script formatting: replace em dashes with hyphens\nfor Keep a Changelog consistency.",
